    "body": "**Verdict change (M5): needs changes before merge.** It supersedes the merge-ready line in the review above. The code fix itself is sound: a ≤1e-9 mm snap, no flips on the slot, island or r6.2 fixtures, and verify verdicts unchanged.\n\nThe blocker is the bore heavy test this PR re-pins: `app pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` **fails on macOS (Apple silicon)** at this head. Measured: moves 16160, planar 15432, arcs 1571. Pinned: 16197 / 15458 / 1581 (`pocket3d_hsm.rs:118`). A test that's red on a supported platform can't merge.\n\nRequested:\n1. Pin the new plan the way #1014 does for the old one: `fell.is_empty()` (Z 20 and Z 10 keep the HSM plan, the real point of this fix), plus moves, planar and arcs in ranges that cover the measured platforms (e.g. moves 16100..=16260, planar 15380..=15520, arcs 1560..=1600). Name both measurements in the decision file.\n2. Reconcile with #1014 (merge-ready), which rewrites the same assertions to ranges for the old plan. Whichever lands second must take the other's form; say in the PR body which order you expect.\n\nTurned back to draft per the review rules.",
